      "math_academy_id": "q-51839",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{9}=9$ and ${a}_{22}=178.$ What is the common difference of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *increasing*, and therefore we expect $d$ to be *positive*.\n\nWe are given the terms\n\n$$\n{a}_{9}=9,\\,{a}_{22}=178.\n$$\n\nTo find $d,$ we apply the formula with $n=22$ and $m=9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{n}-{a}_{m}}{n-m} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{22}-{a}_{9}}{22-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{178-9}{22-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{13} \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=13.$",
